#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:67
msgid ""
"The RiverCure Portal (RCP) brings together geographic contexts, sensor data, "
"and hydrodynamic modeling tools to help manage flood risks. It supports all "
"stages of flood risk management, from assessment and prevention to emergency "
"preparedness and response. The RCP efficiently uses both crowdsourced and "
"authoritative data. This includes curated outputs from sensing instruments "
"and data from virtual entities, which combine lower-level modeling results "
"or other types of information not directly collected by physical instruments."
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:70
msgid ""
"RiverCure addresses the issue of reducing uncertainty and improving "
"forecasting capabilities of hydrodynamic and morphodynamic mathematical "
"models for flood simulation, water resources management and habitat "
"protection."
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:87
msgid "Public Contexts"
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:108
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:123
msgid "What is a Context?"
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:129
msgid ""
"A Context, or geographic Context, refers to a specific geographic area, "
"pertinent to modeling and analyzing flood events. A Context can be linked to "
"a hydrological feature, such as a river, river basin, estuary, or lake. Each "
"context is defined by a name, sensors, and various geographic "
"characteristics."
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:139
msgid ""
"I want to contribute to a Context that does not exist in the RiverCure "
"Portal. What should I do?"
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/about.html:146
#, python-format
msgid ""
"If you wish to contribute to a Context that is not currently defined in the "
"RiverCure Portal, we encourage you to reach out to us through our "
"%(contact)s page. Our team will evaluate your request and respond in a "
"timely manner."
msgstr ""

#: rivercureportal/templates/rivercureportal/contact.html:27
msgid ""
"We appreciate your interest in the RiverCure Portal. Should you have any "
"inquiries, feedback, or require assistance, please complete the form below "
"with your contact information, subject and message. Our team will respond to "
"your submission at the earliest opportunity. Thank you for reaching out to "
"us."
msgstr ""

